    "result_text": "The build is green. The full suite (one test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus its support classes) passes and everything compiles \u2014 including the OpenAPI-generated DTO with the new `GOLD` enum value.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier following the codebase's existing conventions for derived snapshot fields (the same pattern used for `namesakeCount`).\n\n**The rule:** `membershipTier` is `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `householdSize` snapshot field (`household_size` column) with accessors, and made `getMembershipTier()` return `\"GOLD\"` first when `householdSize >= 3`, falling through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic otherwise.\n\n2. **`HouseholdMemberCounter.java`** (new) \u2014 A small single-responsibility `@Component` mirroring `NamesakeCounter`. It counts household members (owners sharing the owner's `householdId`) including the owner itself, reusing the existing `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` lookup \u2014 valid because household members always share a last name (the `householdId` is derived from last name + address). An owner with no `householdId` is a household of one.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 Injected `HouseholdMemberCounter` and stamped `householdSize` in `saveOwner` for new owners, right alongside `customerCode` and `namesakeCount`. This runs after `joinHousehold` has assigned the shared `householdId` and back-filled existing members, so the count reflects the household \"after this create\".\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`) \u2014 Added the `household_size INTEGER` column where the sibling `namesake_count` column already lives (hsqldb drives the test DB; mysql/postgres don't track these derived columns, so I left them as the maintainers had them).\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated its description, so the generated `OwnerDto` accepts the new value.\n\nWalkthrough of the test's 3-member household: member 1 \u2192 size 1, member 2 \u2192 size 2, member 3 \u2192 2 existing members + self = 3 \u2192 `GOLD`. \u2705",
